{#- Three containers on a private Podman network (`network`): paperless
   (web UI, consumer, OCR, task worker — one image, s6-overlay inside),
   postgres and valkey (Celery broker). Only paperless publishes a port;
   postgres/valkey are reachable from that network only, valkey without a
   password (no published port, nothing else on the network) — as netbox.

   uid/gid: the container runs directly as this id (`user:` — upstream's
   rootless mode: no internal UID remapping, USERMAP_UID/GID ignored),
   mapped 1:1 into its user namespace (keep_uids). It owns data_dir here
   and media/consume on the NFS share (root_squash: created as uid via
   setpriv, never :U). Pinned in pillar/paperless.sls users:accounts too.
   Not 1000 (the image's own `paperless` user; on the host that range is
   the per-minion login account).

   media_dir / consume_dir: originals + archive, and the inbox. On the NAS
   share in practice (pillar); consumer_polling_interval > 0 then, since
   NFS delivers no inotify events (seconds, 0 = inotify).

   Secrets (OpenBao via pillar) are written as files to secrets_dir and
   bound one by one into /run/secrets (0444 — the 0700 dir keeps host users
   out), read through upstream's PAPERLESS_<X>_FILE support — never in env,
   so not in `podman inspect`. Written without a trailing newline (the
   image warns, the value would include it). secret_key and db_password
   are required: the formula fails on a blank or unresolved one.

   oidc: login via an OpenID Connect provider (django-allauth). Empty
   server_url = off. Otherwise the provider JSON (incl. the client secret
   oidc_client_secret) becomes a secret file read via
   PAPERLESS_SOCIALACCOUNT_PROVIDERS_FILE. Callback:
   <url>/accounts/oidc/<provider_id>/login/callback/.

   url: the external https URL (PAPERLESS_URL: CSRF origins, links).
   allowed_hosts: extra Host headers accepted besides url's host (the
   upstream probe uses the IP).

   config: extra PAPERLESS_* env, merged over the formula's own (no
   secrets here). dump_dir: where formulas/backup's pre-run pg_dump goes —
   pillar/backup.sls `dumps` repeats this path and postgres_container_name.
   postgres_user / valkey_user: the images' own users (alpine), data dirs
   handed to them by :U. podman / postgres_podman / valkey_podman: spec
   overrides (keys: formulas/podman README). read_only off for paperless
   (s6-overlay writes below /run, scratch in /tmp/paperless) and postgres
   (/run/postgresql) — as netbox. #}
